      "canonical_content_text": "No shock direction exists; all six rows are stand-asides with named H1 levels.\n\nBackground, already in price before the trigger: on 16 Nov SPX fell 2.3% to an H1 low of 7404.58 and WTI fell 3.9% to an H1 low of 83.82; GOLD and EURUSD made lows at 3840.978 and 1.09908; USDJPY and BTCUSD stayed in their bands.\n\nGOLD fell with equities and oil on 16 Nov and USDJPY barely moved on a 2.3% equity fall: the usual haven channels were not active, so the session does not read as a broad flight to safety.\n\nBase case (54%): estimate, BTCUSD is at or below the reference 64451.95 at 2026-11-18T00:37:44Z. Priced: The fall from 73986.7 to the 15 Nov low 61940.88 and two days inside 63829.52 to 65637.9. Positioning: not observed. Zone reason: none; no entry zone is frozen.\nInvalidation reason: a break of the two-day band would show a move this pass did not see.\nConfirmations: none observed.\nInvalidation: A completed H1 bar closes below 63829.52 or above 65637.9. A completed H1 bar that closes below 63829.52 makes a short a candidate for the next pass. A completed H1 bar that closes above 65637.9 removes the short lean. Opposite mechanism: a squeeze through 65637.9 after two days of failed selling.\nMain alternative (46%): estimate, BTCUSD is above 64451.95 at 2026-11-18T00:37:44Z.",
